CBMC reports "template scope 'Tr' not found" (disambiguate_template_classes):
with two packs the pattern's copies are built without Tr's binding, also for
a one-element call.  One pack (`Tr<L>::value...') and a concrete template
(`same<L, R>::value...') work.  The remaining cause of the dropped
__tuple_impl / tuple bodies of cpp20_ranges_basic_libcxx.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
